# Line endings are pinned here, in the repository, rather than left to a
# machine-global core.autocrlf setting.
#
# Why this file exists: every SHA-256 published in hashes.txt is computed over
# LF bytes. evidence/companion_0.4.22_main_beautified.js is listed at 178,366
# bytes, which is its LF length; checked out with CRLF it is 183,764 bytes and
# its hash does not match the published value. Anyone verifying this repository
# on Windows would have found a mismatch and had no way to tell whether the
# cause was line endings or altered evidence. Pinning eol=lf makes every
# checkout byte-identical on every platform, so a published hash reproduces
# anywhere.
#
# This must not depend on core.autocrlf. That setting is per-machine and
# invisible to anyone cloning the repository.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Never convert these, whatever the content sniffing decides.
*.zip   binary
*.exe   binary
*.asar  binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.pdf   binary
